// foresight.storyarc
// part of Arcturus, a programming language and compiler for the Infocom Z-machine.
// Copyright (c) 2026, Stefan Vogt.
// https://github.com/ByteProject/Arcturus
//
// A showcase for summon.foresight: the game does the obvious preparatory
// step for you, and says so in the classic parenthetical. Naming a thing
// at your feet in a command that needs it carried takes it first; a
// closed, unlocked door opens itself on the walk; naming a thing you KNOW
// is inside a closed container opens the container and carries on, the
// steps chaining when they must. The parenthetical is a promise, printed
// only when the repaired step is certain to succeed: locked stays a plain
// refusal, out of reach stays out of reach, and contents you have never
// seen cannot even be named. Off unless summoned; a game without this
// line pays nothing. Compile and run:
//
//   arcc examples/features/foresight.storyarc -o foresight.z5
//   frotz foresight.z5
//
// Try, in order:
//   give coin to ferryman    (taking the brass coin first) and the fare
//                            is paid: the coin was at your feet
//   north                    (first opening the pine door) and you walk
//                            through in one turn
//   get sextant              (opening the display case first): the case
//                            is closed but CLEAR, the sextant plain to
//                            see, so the repair is certain and chained
//   south                    back to the jetty
//   open chest               locked, and foresight NEVER picks locks: a
//                            plain refusal, no parenthetical promises
//   get lantern              the lantern sits in the closed, opaque chest:
//                            never seen, it cannot even be named. The
//                            knowledge rule, working as designed

game
    title  "The Ferry Fare"
    headline "A foresight showcase"
    author "Stefan Vogt"
    start  jetty

summon.statusline
summon.foresight

room jetty
    name "The Jetty"
    desc "Weathered boards over grey water. A pine door leads north into the
          boathouse. The ferryman waits, hand out, endlessly patient."
    north pinedoor

thing coin in jetty
    name "brass coin"
    words coin, >brass
    desc "Fare for one crossing, face worn smooth."

thing ferryman of character in jetty
    name "ferryman"
    words ferryman, ferry, man
    desc "He has seen every excuse and accepts exactly one currency."

    on give coin to self
        say "He bites the coin, nods, and pockets it. You are paid up."

thing chest of container in jetty
    name "sea chest"
    words chest, >sea
    fixed
    openable
    open false
    lockable
    locked
    desc "Iron-strapped and shut. The lock has outlived three keys."

thing lantern in chest
    name "storm lantern"
    words lantern, >storm
    desc "Brass and salt-glass, waiting out its imprisonment."

thing pinedoor of door in jetty, boathouse
    name "pine door"
    words door, >pine
    desc "Pine planks, a thumb latch, no lock at all."

room boathouse
    name "The Boathouse"
    desc "Rope, tar, and one glass display case on a plinth."
    south pinedoor

thing showcase of container in boathouse
    name "display case"
    words case, >display
    fixed
    openable
    open false
    clear
    desc "A glass case on a plinth. The latch is stiff but willing."

thing sextant in showcase
    name "sextant"
    words sextant
    desc "A navigator's sextant, brass arms folded like a sleeping insect."
